    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0663" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.24/12–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-10T20:00:00-05:00">December 10,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2736. Urtel 3594 Dec 4. It was impossible for me to discuss with British
                    Ambassador here<anchor n="88" xml:id="d504-f1"/> activities of representative of
                    British <pb facs="0664" n="650" xml:id="pg650"/> Vickers Armstrong but Assistant
                    Secretary Braden had talk with officer of British Embassy. He expressed grave
                    concern Department about this development on grounds of danger starting armament
                    race and of complicating plans for inter-American defense. British Secretary of
                    Embassy expressed sympathy with Department views and promised to communicate
                    with London and with British Embassy Rio.</p>
                <p>Please take up informally and along same lines with British Ambassador and report
                    by telegram repeating to other four Missions concerned. Department has issued
                    similar instructions in this matter to Embassies London, Rio, Buenos Aires,
                    Santiago and Lima.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d504-f1" n="88" xml:id="d504-f1-content">
